{
  "_comment": [
    "A recorded-SHAPE Razorpay response, not a recording of one.",
    "",
    "Every field name, type and unit here is taken from Razorpay's published",
    "API reference for GET /v1/settlements and GET /v1/settlements/recon/combined.",
    "The VALUES are invented, because generating real ones needs a KYC-activated",
    "merchant account and this exists precisely for the case where there isn't one.",
    "",
    "So this demonstrates that the mapping and the reconciliation work against the",
    "documented contract. It does NOT demonstrate that the contract matches what a",
    "live account returns -- only pointing scripts/pull_razorpay.py at real keys",
    "does that, and verify_tie_out() is the check for it.",
    "",
    "The numbers are constructed so the arithmetic is real: each payment's credit",
    "is gross - fee - tax with fee at 2% and tax at 18% of fee, and the settlement",
    "amount is the exact sum of credit - debit across its own members. One refund",
    "is included because a settlement without one is not a realistic settlement,",
    "and it is the case that breaks a naive mapping.",
    "",
    "settled_at values are unix seconds, as the API returns them."
  ],

